     Hey!  If you're in need of a new challange, or just looking to change 
your priorities why not give this a try:  Try to ascend with the Perfect 
Beast.  
     I got this idea when I was about to ascend with a pet dragon that I'd 
nurtured to 22HD and kept with me the whole game.  He got killed twice though. 
The first time he died I was able to bring him back, but the next time he was 
eaten by another pet.  It seems that dragons don't regenerate very quickly so 
even though he was a force of doom he would slowly die if I didn't keep 
healing him.  Anyway, I was annoyed that I couldn't keep him going the whole 
game so the next time I tried a new approach...
     After getting the WoW in the castle.  I made some wishes, and some piles, 
and after all was said and done I left there with the perfect (almost) woman.  
Her name was Jeanine, and she was a 22nd level Djinni with a -15 AC and a +5 
Vorpal blade who got 3 attacks for the enemy's one (not that it ever took all 
three of them to kill anyone).  Some of her best features were:  A) she could 
fly, so I never lost her to trapdoors. (unless I fell in it, but then I knew 
to get back right away) B) She didn't eat anything, so she could spend all her 
time kicking ass.  C) She didn't draw any fire of her own (I guess no pets do) 
so she could wade through big crowds of monsters without taking any damage.
     Unfortunatley, she lacked one vital item.  That being the item that would 
have kept her from being polymorphed into a soldier ant on the way out.
     Since then I've been experimenting with other pets of doom (Olog-hai's 
work pretty well, well pretty much nothing can kill them anyhow) but still 
haven't taken any all the way.   ;)


